  "limits_and_missing_acceptance_checks": [
    "Probe runs before the 310-second horizon, against synthetic 1/2-root and 2/4/6-root prefixes, not against a rejected step after the evolved late/terminal 310-second state.",
    "The accepted respiration and Brain buffers are byte-compared. Candidate buffers/statuses are allowed to change and the respiration candidate is required to carry failure status; no separate externally named receptor-history buffer is reported.",
    "Displayed state means internal presentation ABI buffers and presentedStep/captured common-coordinate state. The probe does not hash rendered pixels or a video frame around rejection.",
    "Single-reject sameMatterCirculation compares vascularState, vascularClock, controlStep and physicsSubstep. The multi-step comparison additionally checks broad continuation-authoritative Matter arrays; solver/status certificates are intentionally omitted. Neither is a full bytewise rollback of every allocated buffer.",
    "No persisted checkpoint/archive serialization, reload, or archive-identity test is part of this probe. It demonstrates in-memory rejection preservation and replay only; do not claim archive rollback identity.",
    "The build/run receipts pin executable, loaded dylib, shader and data hashes, but do not record a source commit/build manifest. The currently clean source HEAD and probe file hash are review-time source identity, not an attestation that the binary was reproducibly built from that commit."
  ],
